# .dockerignore — the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and .gitignore does NOT
# filter the docker build context. Without this file a local `docker build`
# would bake credentials and dev cruft from the working checkout into the
# pushed image. Pinned by tests/test_ws_b_dockerignore_contract.py — keep the
# two in sync.
#
# ANCHORING — read this before adding a pattern.
#
# Docker matches these patterns against the path relative to the BUILD CONTEXT
# ROOT. `venv/` therefore excludes a top-level `venv` and nothing else; it
# never matched auth_service/venv, which shipped 190 MB and 2763 files in
# every image while a green contract test confirmed the line was present.
# A pattern that must apply at any depth has to say `**/` explicitly. Bare
# names do NOT behave like .gitignore here.
#
# So: anything that is dangerous or worthless wherever it appears is written
# `**/…`. The few patterns deliberately left root-anchored are the top-level
# project layout (tests/, docs/, scripts/, deploy/, test_pdfs/, env/, ENV/) —
# generalising those to any depth would also exclude directories with those
# very common names inside third-party packages.

# --- Credentials / secrets (must never enter an image layer, at any depth) ---
**/service-account*.json
**/*credentials*.json
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/run_production.sh

# --- Local token caches (per-user MSAL/OAuth state, at any depth) ---
**/msal_token_cache.bin
**/token_cache.bin

# --- VCS / CI (vendored checkouts carry their own .git) ---
**/.git
**/.github
**/.gitignore

# --- Tests and test data (not needed at runtime) ---
# Root-anchored on purpose: the project's own suites live at the top level.
tests/
test_pdfs/
**/E2E_TEST_PLAN.md
**/E2E_TEST_RUN_SHEET.md
**/test_results.json

# --- Dev/deploy scaffolding (image is built FROM these, never contains them) ---
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
deploy/
docs/
scripts/
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AI_IMPROVEMENTS_TODO.md
**/*.md

# --- Python / editor / OS cruft ---
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
# Committed virtualenvs. `**/` is load-bearing: auth_service/venv is the one
# that actually exists, and it is not at the context root.
**/venv/
**/.venv/
# Root-anchored: `env` is too common a package directory name to exclude at depth.
env/
ENV/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/logs/

# --- Local data artifacts ---
**/*.xlsx
**/sig.png
